              \"cluster1\": {\n                    \"Destinations\": {\n                        \"cluster1/destination1\": {\n                            \"Address\": \"https://api.github.com/\"\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n","raw_text_sha256":"c3e590ee7d21156843902c9d5584925b21e6a7fedc620b8f3c91800e1bbd1384","source_event_index":3,"source_record_index":3,"source_response_id":"turn_000003","source_turn_text_sha256":"b9be2f4438df895487f526ae5f78c89cb276191139fe52bd428b3df2d0f1c2b4","start_offset":2220,"status":"candidate_requires_semantic_review"},{"candidate_id":"GTC_000003_002869_002884_fed0a11a1e58581e","completeness":"complete","container":"markdown_fence","continuation_status":"none","detector":{"name":"generated-technical-content-v2","version":"2"},"detector_evidence":["complete_standalone_markdown_fence","recognized_fence_label"],"end_offset":2884,"fence_language":"bash","kind":"shell_sequence","legacy_artifact_id":null,"order_within_response":5,"raw_text":"    dotnet run\n","raw_text_sha256":"fed0a11a1e58581e6b1b73c99e712d3fd094e716e5a82bd0b77fe0be1c65454d","source_event_index":3,"source_record_index":3,"source_response_id":"turn_000003","source_turn_text_sha256":"b9be2f4438df895487f526ae5f78c89cb276191139fe52bd428b3df2d0f1c2b4","start_offset":2869,"status":"candidate_requires_semantic_review"}],"identification":{"ambiguity_reason":"","artifact_refs":["GTC_000003_001100_001166_9eb744ce75d11e48","GTC_000003_001262_001308_c7c19a566442edee","GTC_000003_001480_001877_e1dcbf90ffdd66c1","GTC_000003_002220_002792_c3e590ee7d211568","GTC_000003_002869_002884_fed0a11a1e58581e"],"boundary":"exclusive_before:turn_000003","candidate_artifact_ids":["GTC_000003_001100_001166_9eb744ce75d11e48","GTC_000003_001262_001308_c7c19a566442edee","GTC_000003_001480_001877_e1dcbf90ffdd66c1","GTC_000003_002220_002792_c3e590ee7d211568","GTC_000003_002869_002884_fed0a11a1e58581e"],"family_id":"FGF_e01bf1bc654112c019e7e5cc","family_id_provenance":{"algorithm":"sha256","canonical_input":{"artifact_ids":["GTC_000003_001100_001166_9eb744ce75d11e48","GTC_000003_001262_001308_c7c19a566442edee","GTC_000003_001480_001877_e1dcbf90ffdd66c1","GTC_000003_002220_002792_c3e590ee7d211568","GTC_000003_002869_002884_fed0a11a1e58581e"],"case_id":"CASE_2BAC9476B7B1"},"canonicalization":"json-sort-keys-compact-utf8","case_id_included":true,"digest_hex":"e01bf1bc654112c019e7e5ccd7c2915233bcbfac3ed5b7a30c167171dc581149","digest_prefix_length":24},"family_label":"YARP ASP.NET Core reverse-proxy setup and configuration","rationale":"The earliest generated technical-content family appears in turn_000003, directly triggered by turn_000002. Its five candidates coherently form one setup workflow: creating the project, installing YARP, configuring middleware, defining the proxy route and destination, and running the application. Candidates from turn_000005 are later refinements and are excluded.","response_event_index":3,"response_turn_id":"turn_000003","status":"complete","target_prompt_event_index":2,"target_prompt_id":"turn_000002"}},"first_generation_response":{"create_time":1690395187.971202,"event_index":3,"role":"assistant","source_node_id":"949c906b-9694-450d-a012-7f1a23b73003","source_parent_id":"aaa27877-f0a3-40e0-9a5a-798c911fa5d7","source_record_index":3,"text":"YARP (Yet Another Reverse Proxy) is a project from Microsoft that creates a reverse proxy server. A reverse proxy can be used to bypass CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing) restrictions by making requests from the same origin as your website.\n\nCORS is a security measure that prevents a web page from making requests to a different domain than the one from which it came. This is called a cross-origin request. CORS can be bypassed using a reverse proxy, which essentially forwards the request from your domain, making it appear as though it came from the same domain.\n\nPlease note that bypassing CORS restrictions can have serious security implications and should only be done when you have the authority to do so.\n\nTo use YARP to bypass CORS restrictions, you'll need to create a reverse proxy configuration that directs certain requests to the API you're trying to access.\n\nHere's a basic guide to setting up YARP in a .NET 5.0 project to bypass CORS restrictions:\n\n1. **Setup a new ASP.NET Core project:**\n\n    Open your terminal and create a new Web API project using the .NET CLI:\n\n    ```bash\n    dotnet new webapi -n YarpReverseProxy\n    cd YarpReverseProxy\n    ```\n\n2. **Add YARP NuGet package:**\n\n    Add the YARP package to your project:\n\n    ```bash\n    dotnet add package Microsoft.ReverseProxy\n    ```\n\n3. **Configure YARP:**\n\n    Open the `Startup.cs` file and add the YARP services and middleware in the `ConfigureServices` and `Configure` methods:\n\n    ```csharp\n    public void ConfigureServices(IServiceCollection services)\n    {\n        services.AddReverseProxy()\n            .LoadFromConfig(Configuration.GetSection(\"ReverseProxy\"));\n    }\n\n    public void Configure(IApplicationBuilder app, IWebHostEnvironment env)\n    {\n        app.UseRouting();\n        app.UseEndpoints(endpoints =>\n        {\n            endpoints.MapReverseProxy();\n        });\n    }\n    ```\n\n4. **Setup Proxy Config:**\n\n    In `appsettings.json`, you can define the routes and clusters for YARP. A route is a path on your website that should be redirected, and a cluster is a collection of destinations (URLs) that the requests should be forwarded to.\n\n    Here's an example of bypassing CORS for the Github API:\n\n    ```json\n    {\n        \"ReverseProxy\": {\n            \"Routes\": [\n            {\n                \"RouteId\": \"route1\",\n                \"ClusterId\": \"cluster1\",\n                \"Match\": {\n                    \"Path\": \"{**catch-all}\"\n                }\n            }\n            ],\n            \"Clusters\": {\n                \"cluster1\": {\n                    \"Destinations\": {\n                        \"cluster1/destination1\": {\n                            \"Address\": \"https://api.github.com/\"\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    ```\n\n5. **Run the Project:**\n\n    Finally, run the project:\n\n    ```bash\n    dotnet run\n    ```\n\nNow, any requests to your site will be proxied to the Github API, bypassing CORS restrictions. Note that this configuration will proxy all requests. You may want to set up specific routes for different APIs.\n\nPlease remember that the guidelines above are a simple example of how to bypass CORS with YARP. Make sure to follow proper security practices when setting up your reverse proxy.\n\nAs of my knowledge cutoff in September 2021, you may need to check for updates or changes to YARP and .NET.\n","turn_id":"turn_000003"},"target_developer_prompt":{"create_time":1690395137.562048,"event_index":2,"role":"user","source_node_id":"aaa27877-f0a3-40e0-9a5a-798c911fa5d7","source_parent_id":"750321c7-3d17-49b4-8f17-9b732cf49e6d","source_record_index":2,"text":"Can you show me how to use YARP in a project to use it to bypass CORS restrictions on a API?","turn_id":"turn_000002"}},"csv_extraction":{"context":[{"category":"context","evidence_spans":["Can you show me how to use YARP in a project to use it to bypass CORS restrictions on a API?"],"item_id":"context_1","normalized_text":"The task involves using YARP in a project involving an API with CORS restrictions.","source_roles":["user"],"source_turn_ids":["turn_000002"]}],"specificity":[{"category":"specificity","evidence_spans":["Can you show me how to use YARP in a project to use it to bypass CORS restrictions on a API?"],"item_id":"specificity_1","normalized_text":"Show how to use YARP to bypass CORS restrictions on an API.","source_roles":["user"],"source_turn_ids":["turn_000002"]}],"verification":[]},"identity":{"case_id":"CASE_2BAC9476B7B1","conversation_id